{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1118727-micro-template-conjurers-power-born-of-sanity","id":1118727,"title":"[Micro-template] Conjurers - Power born of sanity","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-20T15:42:52-07:00","id":1118727,"title":"[Micro-template] Conjurers - Power born of sanity","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">There are those who say they can pull objects from thin air, call for demons to do their bidding, and command the elements themselves. They\u2019re (largely) full of crap, but there is at least some truth to their rantings. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Conjurers </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>can</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> create items without having the raw materials at hand. But it isn\u2019t from nothing - they spin pieces of their own mind and soul into material being. While this is taxing on their minds, the flexibility it allows is formidable.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Conjurer (Supernatural, \u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></span></b><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>:</b> Integrity, having a soul</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Effect</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>:</b> You\u2019ve figured out how to craft bits of your own soul into material objects. Doing so involves spending a Willpower point and deciding what they wish to create (which may require making an Intelligence + Crafts or other Skill roll) - Conjurers can only create items they could have otherwise made themselves, given the time and materials. Each such item, or group of items, created requires \u201cinvesting\u201d at least one point of Integrity per Size (reducing Integrity by that amount, to a minimum of 1), though the final Size and other characteristics (such as Armor, Durability, or Equipment Bonuses) are limited to no higher than your dots in this merit. You can reclaim your Integrity by banishing the item as an Instant action.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Drawback</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>:</b> Other than lowering your Integrity while your Conjured items are in existence, if those creations are destroyed, you roll a number of Breaking Points equal to the Integrity invested in the item.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <u><b>Other Merits:</b></u></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Flash Conjuration (\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Prerequisites</b>: Conjurer \u2022, Wits \u2022\u2022\u2022</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Effect</b>: You can now spin things into existence at a moment\u2019s notice, Conjuring as a Reflexive action.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Drawback</b>: Unfortunately, swiftly made, swiftly fade - anything Conjured as a Reflexive action only lasts 1 Turn before automatically being dismissed.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Efficient Conjuration (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Prerequisites</b>: Conjurer \u2022\u2022</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Effect</b>: You can extend the bits of your soul further than other Conjurers. For each dot in this merit, you can support one more Size, bonus, or other value for your Conjurations without Investing additional Integrity. Each Conjuration still requires a minimum of 1 Integrity, and still cannot have a value higher than your dots in Conjurer.<br /> <br /> <b>Expanded Conjuration (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Conjurer \u2022<br /> <b>Effect:</b> You are able to exceed the normal dimensions of your talent, Conjuring larger items. For each dot in this merit, you can Conjure objects 1 Size larger than your normal limit as determined by your Conjurer dots. You still must bind 1 Integrity per Size, as normal, for these creations.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Triflings (\u2022)</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Prerequisites</b>: Conjurer \u2022\u2022</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Effect</b>: You grant a bit of permanency to the least of your creations. Once per Scene, you can create a small amount of disposable materials (such as screws, bits of bread, or bullets) of cumulative Size 1. These do not require investing any Integrity, but must be used by the end of the Scene and cannot have notable material worth (Availability of the items is limited to 1, or 2 in rare cases).</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Pyrotechnics (\u2022\u2022)</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Prerequisites</b>: Conjurer \u2022</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Effect</b>: You can now Conjurer forms of energy, like flame and light, sustaining them through means of your power (and soul) alone. The force will persist until dismissed, though any consequences (such as material ignited through Conjured fire) will persist even after the original source is dismissed.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Gift of Life (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Prerequisites</b>: Conjurer \u2022, Medicine \u2022, Animal Ken \u2022</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Effect</b>: You can now call forth living creatures from the depths of your being. Create an animal no more than Conjurer in Size, and with Attributes and Skills capped at that threshold as well.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Note</b>: The animal is generally typical for its type, within the limits imposed above, and usually well disposed toward its creator. Other than its continued existence, no special bond exists between animal and Conjurer, and Animal Ken is necessary to get it to perform atypical actions.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Material Servant (\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Prerequisites</b>: Conjurer \u2022\u2022\u2022</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Effects</b>: You can invest Integrity into an item, creating a Retainer equal to the amount of Integrity invested. Roll Wits + Occult. For each success, you can give the Retainer one command it will follow (such as &quot;fetch me a towel&quot; for one Success, or &quot;Pick up water from this well, then dump it in that basin. And then stop once the basin is full&quot; for 3 Successes).</span></span> <hr /><br /> [Notes for other ideas]<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I<b>nvisible Stalker (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b> </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Prerequisites</b>: Conjurer \u2022\u2022\u2022</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Effect</b>: [Create a Rank 1 Ghost and assign it a task. Its Anchors are you and the task. Attributes and Essence are capped at the amount of Integrity invested.]</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mortar of Will - Patches and reinforces an object? Cheaper than creating it whole-cloth? Can add Tags to existing items?</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mortar the Flesh - Can add Health boxes. And/Or restore missing limbs?</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Eldritch Whispers - Can \u201ccreate\u201d metaphysical and mental things, like Clues, Plans, and knowledge representing Equipment Bonuses. But you get a Condition like Guilty or Obsessed from the supernatural information.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Eldritch Lore - Can add Skills and Specializations. Gain Impostor Condition or similar?</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Eldritch Secrets - Can trade Integrity for Supernatural Merits (up to Conjurer in dots for any one Merit per instance). They keep their Drawbacks.</span></span> <hr /><br /> I'll edit and expand this post as I iron out more ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 07-25-2017, 06:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T17:03:26-07:00","id":1118762,"title":"","content":"Nice. Looking forward to what you have in store.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T21:35:51-07:00","id":1118831,"title":"","content":"As far as I can tell, there's no limitation on complexity. If I've got Conjurer \u2022, it looks like I could generate a Size 1 hunk of solid platinum or a copy of the Mona Lisa. Heck, couldn't I just conjure something that's not technically possible, like a copy of tomorrow's New York Tribune (or the formula for the cure for cancer)?<br /> <br /> I mean, this is <i>incredibly</i> bare-bones, but... I'm not exactly getting what makes these guys a micro-template, rather than just being a Supernatural merit that has a bunch of other merits that require it.<br /> <br /> If you look at other micro-templates, they tend to work on a basis of &quot;merit + mechanical gimmick&quot;:<br /> <br /> \u2022 The Dreamers and Psychic Vampires have their own fuel stats - heck, Dreamers have a pair of unique conditions.<br /> \u2022 The Infected have a Condition chain that their merits all build off of.<br /> \u2022 Lost Boys have powers that fluctuate based off of when their last hit of sweet, sweet Neuropozyne was.<br /> \u2022 The Plain suffer Breaking Points from observing violence, let alone participating in it.<br /> \u2022 Stigmatics get a Catastrophic Glitch, forcibly marking them as different.<br /> <br /> The one exception that I can think of is the Atariya... but I also think that it's one of the weakest official minor templates.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> Ultimately, what makes these guys <i>Conjurers</i>, and not just guys who can make things pop into existence?<br /> <br /> A good template can't be ignored - even if you stop using your cool powers, you still can't avoid that, hey, you're a sleeper agent (or a cyborg, or the vector of a mystical plague, etc). Meanwhile, a Conjurer could just... choose not to conjure things anymore. Heck, they have more choice in the matter than someone who with Psychokinesis, and no-one's calling Psychokinetics their own minor template.<br /> <br /> What makes this a <i>thing you are</i>, instead of just a cool trick?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T22:33:32-07:00","id":1118837,"title":"","content":"Are conjurers <i>not</i> people who are defined by their ability to just make things pop into existence?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T23:23:06-07:00","id":1118848,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=ArcaneArts;n1118837]Are conjurers <i>not</i> people who are defined by their ability to just make things pop into existence?[/QUOTE<br /> <br /> That's... not really my problem with this (probably a problem with how I <i>communicated</i> my problem, however).<br /> <br /> If I were to rename Psychokinesis to Psychokinetic (and packaged it with all of the &quot;upgrade&quot; merits from Hurt Locker), would I be justified in calling it a micro-template? Because that's essentially what this is - Conjurer (with maybe a rename) wouldn't be too amiss next to Apportation, Telekinesis, or Telepathy as just a straight Supernatural merit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T02:39:14-07:00","id":1118875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1118727-micro-template-conjurers-power-born-of-sanity?p=1118831#post1118831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as I can tell, there's no limitation on complexity. If I've got Conjurer \u2022, it looks like I could generate a Size 1 hunk of solid platinum or a copy of the Mona Lisa. Heck, couldn't I just conjure something that's not technically possible, like a copy of tomorrow's New York Tribune (or the formula for the cure for cancer)?</div> </div> </div> </div>I clarified a bit (specifically what the Intelligence + Skill roll was called for). Conjurers can only create what they could otherwise do so with time and materials (Integrity handles the materials, and Willpower handles the time).<br /> <br /> So, they could only replicate a Size 1 Mona Lisa if they could make a reasonable forgery (in which case, why don't they?), and tomorrow's Newspaper or the cure for cancer are limited to their own ability to write or invent them (again, why don't they?). They certainly <i>can</i> create a Size 1 chunk of platinum (provided they know what platinum is). <br /> <br /> Of course, for all these things, they exist only so long as the Conjurer invests Integrity into them. They reclaim that Integrity, or the item gets irrevocably altered? It vanishes (and they roll Breaking Points if it was &quot;destroyed&quot; doing so). Pay someone Conjurered money and then dismiss it once you leave? You can, but what you paid them ends up &quot;missing&quot;. Great for cons, not so much for getting rich without incident.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1118727-micro-template-conjurers-power-born-of-sanity?p=1118831#post1118831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, this is <i>incredibly</i> bare-bones, but... I'm not exactly getting what makes these guys a micro-template, rather than just being a Supernatural merit that has a bunch of other merits that require it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It <i>is</i> still a work-in-progress. I just posted what I have so far because it is usable.<br /> <br /> From what I recall, a Micro template, as opposed to a Minor template, is really nothing more than a thematic merit chain.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1118727-micro-template-conjurers-power-born-of-sanity?p=1118831#post1118831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ultimately, what makes these guys <i>Conjurers</i>, and not just guys who can make things pop into existence?<br /> <br /> A good template can't be ignored - even if you stop using your cool powers, you still can't avoid that, hey, you're a sleeper agent (or a cyborg, or the vector of a mystical plague, etc). Meanwhile, a Conjurer could just... choose not to conjure things anymore. Heck, they have more choice in the matter than someone who with Psychokinesis, and no-one's calling Psychokinetics their own minor template.<br /> <br /> What makes this a <i>thing you are</i>, instead of just a cool trick?</div> </div> </div> </div>Working on that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T02:47:03-07:00","id":1118877,"title":"","content":"True but i like conjurer its cool and im going 2 use it hopefully my storyteller will alow me 2 cure cancer","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13426-ameraaaaaa","name":"Ameraaaaaa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T02:58:24-07:00","id":1118880,"title":"","content":"How does the Triflings merit interact with the notion of gold or platinum screws?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T03:30:50-07:00","id":1118888,"title":"","content":"i see only things they can make themselves this is great and balanced if i play a croseover gam them other then a hunter or mage or mummy or devent or ghost or changeling or purefied or lost boys or sorcerer then i'd play this and i know that's a lot but that's because there so good not because this is bad oh not counting some fan made micros on this vary site<br /> and i was notnaming them in order","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13426-ameraaaaaa","name":"Ameraaaaaa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T03:39:48-07:00","id":1118889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1118727-micro-template-conjurers-power-born-of-sanity?p=1118880#post1118880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does the Triflings merit interact with the notion of gold or platinum screws?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Good point. I need to add a limitation for high value objects to that one. It is <i>meant</i> to let a Conjurer create things like bullets, arrows, or small bits of food without tanking their Integrity. Might have to scrap the whole merit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 07-21-2017, 06:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T03:50:07-07:00","id":1118890,"title":"","content":"Damn if you're taking this away then never mind about them being cool i realize a nage is able 2 do this better","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13426-ameraaaaaa","name":"Ameraaaaaa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T03:52:28-07:00","id":1118892,"title":"","content":"What you could do is have the concept of &quot;triflings&quot; be based on the character's intent. If they are literally just going to make some stuff to throw away like bullets it's fine, but the notion &quot;I am going to make lots of little expensive things and sell them&quot; makes them not count because it would leave behind a tangible existence in the money. <br /> <br /> This would let you make silver bullets as long as you intend to load them into a gun and shoot a werewolf, but not if you plan to sell them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T03:57:19-07:00","id":1118893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ameraaaaaa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1118727-micro-template-conjurers-power-born-of-sanity?p=1118890#post1118890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Damn if you're taking this away then never mind about them being cool i realize a nage is able 2 do this better</div> </div> </div> </div>In that case you could skip on all the minor templates and most if not all Supernatural Merits because mages are able to do all of those better.<br /> <br /> <br /> I see that the Merits doesn't take the Availability rating into account. Triflings could be stuff that has an Availability rating of 1 (or less) on top of the other limitations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T04:06:26-07:00","id":1118896,"title":"","content":"Actually reading again it's not clear how size 0 items work. Is there just always a minimum of 1 integrity cost? That seems most logical.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T04:55:43-07:00","id":1118908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1118727-micro-template-conjurers-power-born-of-sanity?p=1118896#post1118896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually reading again it's not clear how size 0 items work. Is there just always a minimum of 1 integrity cost? That seems most logical.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems logical, but then you should be able to create a bunch of the stuff up to a combined Size of 1. Instead of one nail it's a packet of nails. Or maybe that removes some of the useability of Triflings.<br /> <br /> I think it's better to not roll Breaking Points more than once. I think it's already a general rule (or a common houserule) to just roll the worst Breaking Point the character is exposed to in a scene, and rolling the same thing multiple times is generally bad design. Rather, I think only one Breaking Point should be rolled but with a penalty equal to the Integrity dots spent in the destroyed object.<br /> \u200b<br /> I'd also like to see a clarification of Invisible Servant before I can comment on that and Invisible Stalker.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T05:14:25-07:00","id":1118912,"title":"","content":"I think the idea is that you stand a chance to lose <i>all</i> the integrity points invested in a destroyed item. The breaking point rolls determine how many make it back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T05:22:08-07:00","id":1118914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1118727-micro-template-conjurers-power-born-of-sanity?p=1118892#post1118892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What you could do is have the concept of &amp;quot;triflings&amp;quot; be based on the character's intent. If they are literally just going to make some stuff to throw away like bullets it's fine, but the notion &amp;quot;I am going to make lots of little expensive things and sell them&amp;quot; makes them not count because it would leave behind a tangible existence in the money. <br /> <br /> This would let you make silver bullets as long as you intend to load them into a gun and shoot a werewolf, but not if you plan to sell them.</div> </div> </div> </div>How about used or consumed by the end of the Scene? Silver Bullets - fire them that scene. Candy - eat it that Scene. Screws - reuse Triflings or whatever it is falls apart next Scene.<br /> <br /> I might just throw in the intent or Availability restriction if this doesn't fit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1118727-micro-template-conjurers-power-born-of-sanity?p=1118896#post1118896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually reading again it's not clear how size 0 items work. Is there just always a minimum of 1 integrity cost? That seems most logical.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. I'll add some clarifying text to that effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T05:25:17-07:00","id":1118915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1118727-micro-template-conjurers-power-born-of-sanity?p=1118912#post1118912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the idea is that you stand a chance to lose <i>all</i> the integrity points invested in a destroyed item. The breaking point rolls determine how many make it back.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. Something just effectively shattered a portion of your mind/soul, and you get to see how much you can scavenge back.<br /> <br /> I suppose it could be &quot;roll invested Integrity and get Successes back (capped at investment)&quot; but that wouldn't integrate into the other Breaking Point related rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T05:33:34-07:00","id":1118918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1118727-micro-template-conjurers-power-born-of-sanity?p=1118908#post1118908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd also like to see a clarification of Invisible Servant before I can comment on that and Invisible Stalker.</div> </div> </div> </div>Still working on it, but the basic idea is you get a Retainer of [invested Integrity] dots, that you can issue a few orders to. Fetch me a towel, carry these buckets of water, trail that guy. That sort of thing.<br /> <br /> Stalker upgrades that to an actual stat'd (if temporary... most likely) ephemeral. Which can do the above, <i>and</i> push someone down the stairs or something. Probably a Rank 1 Ghost, mechanically (with Conjurer and target as Anchors).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 07-21-2017, 08:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T05:38:40-07:00","id":1118923,"title":"","content":"Is the Servant also ephemeral?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T05:45:38-07:00","id":1118926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1118727-micro-template-conjurers-power-born-of-sanity?p=1118923#post1118923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the Servant also ephemeral?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes? I'm not sure. I was thinking so, but which type? Does it matter? How would a material servant work? Disney's Beauty and the Beast or the Sorcerer's Apprentice style?<br /> <br /> Still thinking that section out. I am open to suggestions, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T05:55:37-07:00","id":1118928,"title":"","content":"Well, the problem with ephemeral entities is that they can't affect the material world except through Manifestations and certain Numina, and that requires systems not suited for the Retainer Merit. I'm all for creating servants, but it might be better to have it be two separate Merits where one is Invisible Stalker (a goetic-like entity that scouts and spies for you but doesn't have any Manifestations or Numina) and one that is material. Perhaps something akin to the Life 4 spell Golem from Mage. Both could then be represented by the Retainer Merit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T06:05:38-07:00","id":1118931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1118727-micro-template-conjurers-power-born-of-sanity?p=1118928#post1118928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the problem with ephemeral entities is that they can't affect the material world except through Manifestations and certain Numina, and that requires systems not suited for the Retainer Merit. I'm all for creating servants, but it might be better to have it be two separate Merits where one is Invisible Stalker (a goetic-like entity that scouts and spies for you but doesn't have any Manifestations or Numina) and one that is material. Perhaps something akin to the Life 4 spell Golem from Mage. Both could then be represented by the Retainer Merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could do that. Leave actual Manifestations and Numina Ephemerals to an Advanced version.<br /> <br /> I was originally thinking like an almost self-driven Telekinesis-like force. It could do simple tasks, but is command directed instead of directly controlled like TK.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T14:06:53-07:00","id":1119069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1118727-micro-template-conjurers-power-born-of-sanity?p=1118928#post1118928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the problem with ephemeral entities is that they can't affect the material world except through Manifestations and certain Numina, and that requires systems not suited for the Retainer Merit. I'm all for creating servants, but it might be better to have it be two separate Merits where one is Invisible Stalker (a goetic-like entity that scouts and spies for you but doesn't have any Manifestations or Numina) and one that is material. Perhaps something akin to the Life 4 spell Golem from Mage. Both could then be represented by the Retainer Merit.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I updated to include Material Servant. Still ironing out Invisible Stalker. I'm probably going to go with Ghost as the mechanical template, due to actually having Manifestations (like Twilight Form) to build off of. I might add a Goetic variant for sending out into the dream/mind-scape in search of information. Or harassment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T14:12:16-07:00","id":1119071,"title":"","content":"Twilight Form is the default for all ephemeral entities and shouldn't be considered a Manifestation. The books certainly don't treat it as a Manifestation, which is why it's not mentioned for Goetia despite them having it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T18:00:01-07:00","id":1120171,"title":"","content":"I'm thinking of making Conjuration call for an Intelligence + Crafts (or Science, or Chemistry, or whatever) roll, with Exceptional Success either giving the resultant item some nice Tag/Condition, or refunding the Willpower point. More complicated creations would penalize the roll (simple stuff is no penalty, Conjuring a complex mechanism, such as a computer or gun, or exacting details, such as a painting, would be -1 to -5).<br /> <br /> I'm also thinking of establishing a range as well. Something like Wits * 5 yards or something?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T18:51:16-07:00","id":1120179,"title":"","content":"An idea:<br /> <br /> Their dots in Conjurer also act as a cap on, essentially, how many merit dots something is worth.<br /> <br /> Unless you want Conjurers to produce platinum ingots as a basic &quot;thing&quot; they can do, you could say that they end up with, I dunno, [Conjurer Dots/2 + 2] worth of Cash, rounded up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-25T02:00:49-07:00","id":1120271,"title":"","content":"Well they're outdone by anyone who can just make the thing other then the merit that can make plans and the 1 that can make skill dots or something like that i don't see the benefit other then being able to make it on the fly planing ahead makes it useless but plans are really free dice and skill dits are great a few other merits interesting so yeah i think mage would make redundant if weren't for paradox and the ability to use it for plan's and skill dots so yeah but conjurer have to use integrity so yeah what's wrose paradox or maybe losing integrity","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13426-ameraaaaaa","name":"Ameraaaaaa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-25T03:14:46-07:00","id":1120282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1118727-micro-template-conjurers-power-born-of-sanity?p=1120179#post1120179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An idea:<br /> <br /> Their dots in Conjurer also act as a cap on, essentially, how many merit dots something is worth.<br /> <br /> Unless you want Conjurers to produce platinum ingots as a basic &quot;thing&quot; they can do, you could say that they end up with, I dunno, [Conjurer Dots/2 + 2] worth of Cash, rounded up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Conjurer dots already cap total bonuses (as well as Size), so for the Platinum, I'd compare it to an equivalent Cash equipment. Conjurer 1? Cash \u2022. Conjurer 5? Cash (or equivalent) \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022. I might need to tinker with the final totals though, depending on consequences.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ameraaaaaa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1118727-micro-template-conjurers-power-born-of-sanity?p=1120271#post1120271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well they're outdone by anyone who can just make the thing other then the merit that can make plans and the 1 that can make skill dots or something like that i don't see the benefit other then being able to make it on the fly planing ahead makes it useless but plans are really free dice and skill dits are great a few other merits interesting so yeah i think mage would make redundant if weren't for paradox and the ability to use it for plan's and skill dots so yeah but conjurer have to use integrity so yeah what's wrose paradox or maybe losing integrity</div> </div> </div> </div>Bear in mind Conjurers of sufficient power can make nearly <i>anything*</i> that is needed in an Instant Action. Could an artist paint a masterpiece? In days. The same skilled Conjurer can do it in <i>seconds</i>. Granted painting it the old-fashioned way doesn't strain one's mind/sanity/soul, but hey, trade offs.<br /> <br /> A Conjurer, if captured, can be deprived of all weapons and tools, stuck somewhere, then proceed to recreate all their weapons and tools. They are never really unarmed*, never without the necessary equipment*, and with Flash Conjuration, they can even generate instant cover against gunfire.<br /> <br /> The Conjurer's problem is when they rely on their powers too much and something inevitably happens to break their toys - which correspondingly cracks their mind. But they are probably too used to their behavior, so all it does is start a downward spiral into them being a broken, powerless shell.<br /> <br /> * = Given that the Conjurer has the appropriate skills to know what they are doing. Which they are encouraged to learn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 07-25-2017, 06:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-25T03:25:17-07:00","id":1120284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1118727-micro-template-conjurers-power-born-of-sanity?p=1118848#post1118848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1118727-micro-template-conjurers-power-born-of-sanity?p=1118837#post1118837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are conjurers <i>not</i> people who are defined by their ability to just make things pop into existence?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's... not really my problem with this (probably a problem with how I <i>communicated</i> my problem, however).<br /> <br /> If I were to rename Psychokinesis to Psychokinetic (and packaged it with all of the &quot;upgrade&quot; merits from Hurt Locker), would I be justified in calling it a micro-template? Because that's essentially what this is - Conjurer (with maybe a rename) wouldn't be too amiss next to Apportation, Telekinesis, or Telepathy as just a straight Supernatural merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about a similar Power Incontinence Drawback for Conjurers? At 0 Willpower, they end up subconsciously creating all kinds of minor, inconvenient crap everywhere?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-25T04:02:01-07:00","id":1120292,"title":"","content":"Well the amount of drowbacks make it unattractive plus if they can catch you why not kill them just saying mage dos this alot better when i made banes that you can find in the brotherhood thread they have something that no other template has nearly true immortalty they can survive a nuke yet it's there only power plus has 3 weeknesses now in a crossover that is where these things tend to be used that has apeal","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13426-ameraaaaaa","name":"Ameraaaaaa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-25T05:19:55-07:00","id":1120317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ameraaaaaa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1118727-micro-template-conjurers-power-born-of-sanity?p=1120292#post1120292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well the amount of drowbacks make it unattractive, plus if they can catch you, why not kill them?<br /> just saying mage dos this alot better.<br /> when i made banes that you can find in the brotherhood thread they have something that no other template has - nearly true immortalty. they can survive a nuke, yet it's there only power. plus has 3 weeknesses now in a crossover that is where these things tend to be used that has apeal</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course Mage is going to be more impressive. It's Mage, and a full template as well. This is a Micro-Template - as in, still close to mortal. They shouldn't be outdoing the major templates. Is a Psychic Vampire superior to the Kindred?<br /> <br /> As for they &quot;why capture when they can just kill them?&quot; - I'm guessing you don't have jails or prisons in your settings. Or hostages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 07-25-2017, 08:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-25T19:59:29-07:00","id":1120601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1118727-micro-template-conjurers-power-born-of-sanity?p=1120317#post1120317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for they &quot;why capture when they can just kill them?&quot; - I'm guessing you don't have jails or prisons in your settings. Or hostages.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or people who, you know, just don't like killing. Which would be... the grand majority of the population.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Anyway, I'd like to point out the near-perfect partnership between a Conjurer and a <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1048533-minor-template-take-two-the-family-titov\">Titov</a>.<br /> <br /> Turns out bribery powers go <i>really well</i> with make-stuff powers. Plus, they both have a &quot;your power comes at a cost of sanity&quot; theme, so they'll have some common ground there.<br /> <br /> On to the merits...<br /> <br /> Eldritch Lore/Whispers/Secrets don't feel <i>right</i>, as far as &quot;conjuring stuff&quot; powers go. It kind of dilutes the idea of &quot;summoning&quot; if you can <i>also</i> come up with brilliant plans on-the-spot and can read minds.<br /> <br /> I mean, I can kind of see a <i>way</i> of &quot;refactoring&quot; the merits to make them work.<br /> <br /> <b>Conjurer:</b> By &quot;investing&quot; a dot in Integrity, you can create things whose Size and equipment bonus are limited to your dots in this merit. These things...<br /> 1) Must be independent objects.<br /> 2) Must be inanimate.<br /> 3) Cannot be supernatural.<br /> 4) Cannot contain information that you, yourself, don't know (no perfect audio recordings of the Gettysburg Address unless you've <i>actually</i> heard what Lincoln's voice sounded like, and no maps of places you've never been)<b>.</b><br /> 5) Must be inorganic - steel and plastic are fine, leather isn't.<br /> <br /> <b>Merit #1:</b> Lets you conjure things as part of something else, letting you do things like replacing a fuse by tapping the fusebox or replace the engine of your car. The overall object needs to follow all the other restrictions other than size/equipment bonus (you can repair your supercomputer, even if you only have Conjurer \u2022).<br /> <br /> <b>Merit #2:</b> You can give your creations life/motive force. At the <i>very least</i>, you can do Mickey-Mouse <i>Fantasia</i> garbage.<br /> <br /> <b>Merit #3:</b> You can make supernatural stuff now. Lets your items mimic the effects of some supernatural merits, or even Dread Powers if you're good enough.<br /> <br /> <b>Merit #4:</b> Your creations can know things that you don't. Conjure up a flawless map of somewhere you've never been, pull a phone book out of nowhere, or just conjure up a copy of <i>Doom</i> to play during downtime.<br /> <br /> <b>Merit #5:</b> You guessed it - you can do organic stuff now. At the <i>very</i> least, you can make some fine leather jackets.<br /> <br /> The real fun, of course, being that you can <i>combine</i> those upgrade merits. Merits #1 and #5 could let you replace someone's arm, you can make homunculi with Merits #2, #4, and #5...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T02:52:55-07:00","id":1120713,"title":"","content":"I think a micro template should make up for there lack of power by not having as much weeknesses sence micro templates seem to me mostly for crossovers <br /> I like anechas version it has enough meet to it that i would use it for a crossover as long as you maybe get rid of the integrity cost but is ok with it im fine still might use it after all it's cool","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13426-ameraaaaaa","name":"Ameraaaaaa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T15:20:31-07:00","id":1121047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1118727-micro-template-conjurers-power-born-of-sanity?p=1120601#post1120601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, I'd like to point out the near-perfect partnership between a Conjurer and a <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1048533-minor-template-take-two-the-family-titov\">Titov</a>.<br /> <br /> Turns out bribery powers go <i>really well</i> with make-stuff powers. Plus, they both have a &quot;your power comes at a cost of sanity&quot; theme, so they'll have some common ground there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was actually thinking they would also combo well with the Doubly Soul'd (or whatever their name is), due to artificially inflating Integrity through others' souls.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1118727-micro-template-conjurers-power-born-of-sanity?p=1120601#post1120601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On to the merits...<br /> <br /> Eldritch Lore/Whispers/Secrets don't feel <i>right</i>, as far as &quot;conjuring stuff&quot; powers go. It kind of dilutes the idea of &quot;summoning&quot; if you can <i>also</i> come up with brilliant plans on-the-spot and can read minds.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the idea was that they move from conjuring items to conjuring metaphysical things, like knowledge or occult secrets. I'm just wondering what the attendant downside should be - putting up a spiritual Craigslist Ad (&quot;Desperate Conjurer seeks Firearms Knowledge. Accepting any offer.&quot;) should have some consequences.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1118727-micro-template-conjurers-power-born-of-sanity?p=1120601#post1120601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, I can kind of see a <i>way</i> of &quot;refactoring&quot; the merits to make them work.<br /> <br /> <b>Conjurer:</b> By &quot;investing&quot; a dot in Integrity, you can create things whose Size and equipment bonus are limited to your dots in this merit. These things...<br /> 1) Must be independent objects.<br /> 2) Must be inanimate.<br /> 3) Cannot be supernatural.<br /> 4) Cannot contain information that you, yourself, don't know (no perfect audio recordings of the Gettysburg Address unless you've <i>actually</i> heard what Lincoln's voice sounded like, and no maps of places you've never been)<b>.</b><br /> 5) Must be inorganic - steel and plastic are fine, leather isn't.<br /> <br /> <b>Merit #1:</b> Lets you conjure things as part of something else, letting you do things like replacing a fuse by tapping the fusebox or replace the engine of your car. The overall object needs to follow all the other restrictions other than size/equipment bonus (you can repair your supercomputer, even if you only have Conjurer \u2022).<br /> <br /> <b>Merit #2:</b> You can give your creations life/motive force. At the <i>very least</i>, you can do Mickey-Mouse <i>Fantasia</i> garbage.<br /> <br /> <b>Merit #3:</b> You can make supernatural stuff now. Lets your items mimic the effects of some supernatural merits, or even Dread Powers if you're good enough.<br /> <br /> <b>Merit #4:</b> Your creations can know things that you don't. Conjure up a flawless map of somewhere you've never been, pull a phone book out of nowhere, or just conjure up a copy of <i>Doom</i> to play during downtime.<br /> <br /> <b>Merit #5:</b> You guessed it - you can do organic stuff now. At the <i>very</i> least, you can make some fine leather jackets.<br /> <br /> The real fun, of course, being that you can <i>combine</i> those upgrade merits. Merits #1 and #5 could let you replace someone's arm, you can make homunculi with Merits #2, #4, and #5...</div> </div> </div> </div>So, in this model, all Conjurations just cost just 1 Integrity. Initial Conjurations are limited to solid-ish, inorganic objects. Merits let you Conjure complex objects, moving things, supernatural items, organic stuff, and crap you don't know, but can name?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ameraaaaaa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1118727-micro-template-conjurers-power-born-of-sanity?p=1120713#post1120713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think a micro template should make up for there lack of power by not having as much weeknesses sence micro templates seem to me mostly for crossovers<br /> I like anechas version it has enough meet to it that i would use it for a crossover as long as you maybe get rid of the integrity cost but is ok with it im fine still might use it after all it's cool</div> </div> </div> </div>These don't have that much weakness. But without the Integrity risk (not cost, unless you break or use up your Conjurations) there is no limit to how much you can create. Which will rapidly break challenges and the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T19:39:01-07:00","id":1121155,"title":"","content":"You're thinking of <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1105930-minor-template-ish-doubly-soul-d\">Soul Takers</a>.<br /> <br /> I didn't list any drawbacks in the model I've advanced - it could be as severe as costing an extra dot of Integrity for each upgrade, or you could just use the Strain condition to represent it being harsher on them than normal if you want a milder drawback.<br /> <br /> The problem with having a bunch of different conditions is that it gets... hectic... if you have too many going at once.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T20:02:01-07:00","id":1121160,"title":"","content":"Wrong thread post","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":".  Wrong thread 07-26-2017, 11:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T08:17:08-07:00","id":1124786,"title":"","content":"So, do you have any concrete ideas or just plot hooks for how people become Conjurers? Is it some sort of Enlightenment Superpower unlocked through the right training in the right places? Is it something you're born with like some Supernatural Merits? Is it provided by a magical relic or patron?<br /> <br /> I know I could make up my own answer, but I prefer solid, but vague plot hooks to build on like Amechra's mysterious Hammer Men who give the Spike Men their cursed abilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T10:16:17-07:00","id":1124824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1118727-micro-template-conjurers-power-born-of-sanity?p=1124786#post1124786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, do you have any concrete ideas or just plot hooks for how people become Conjurers? Is it some sort of Enlightenment Superpower unlocked through the right training in the right places? Is it something you're born with like some Supernatural Merits? Is it provided by a magical relic or patron?<br /> <br /> I know I could make up my own answer, but I prefer solid, but vague plot hooks to build on like Amechra's mysterious Hammer Men who give the Spike Men their cursed abilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thinking. It wouldn't be provided by a Relic or patron. I kinda want them more disconnected than that. It might be a mix of inborn talent and training. Accidentally discovering it should be possible.<br /> <br /> I'm thinking about hooks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}